From 17c18839387d628dc8837456dd79ec852c0589c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 14:01:41 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Nested ocean: net_inflow pins the net inflow through the open
 sides

nested_ocean_model(parent, grid; net_inflow, net_inflow_depth_exponent). At every barotropic substep, after the Flather
fill, one correction over all open faces sets their net inflow to net_inflow (a number or a Ref), as the volume
constraints of NEMO and ROMS do (Oceananigans NetInflow, CliMA/Oceananigans.jl#6524); the split between the sides is
left to Flather. The parent's depth means are shifted by one common velocity so that the exterior transport carries
the same net inflow. The pin's shift of each column is proportional to H^net_inflow_depth_exponent (default 0: the same
transport per unit length; 1: the same velocity; 1/2: the same exterior sea level in Flather).

The test is skipped until an Oceananigans release has NetInflow (TODO in the test).

Rebuilt on the current ss/nested-ocean-model (#676) from e22c1bfd: the exchanger's shift of the depth means now runs
in sample_bands!, after each sampling of the parent.

